1
00:01:00,359 --> 00:01:01,679
Then the two of you worked together

2
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:03,960
to drag the body into the rental.

3
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,280
You must remember it well:

4
00:01:09,239 --> 00:01:10,480
how you used tools to dismember the body,

5
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:13,480
how you wrapped it in plastic sheeting.

6
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:15,280
Except for one thing:

7
00:01:16,319 --> 00:01:18,519
Zhang Weihong's performance impressed you.

8
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:20,599
And so the case became

9
00:01:22,359 --> 00:01:23,840
a family of three

10
00:01:24,599 --> 00:01:25,439
who vanished,

11
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:27,560
never to be found again.

12
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:31,439
Zhang Weihong told me

13
00:01:32,239 --> 00:01:33,560
she would never betray me.

14
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:34,879
She didn't betray you.

15
00:01:35,519 --> 00:01:36,959
You just overestimated yourself.

16
00:01:39,879 --> 00:01:40,879
You wanted to control her

17
00:01:41,359 --> 00:01:42,439
and control the family fortune.

18
00:01:44,840 --> 00:01:45,840
But you never expected

19
00:01:47,599 --> 00:01:48,959
that once the family vanished,

20
00:01:49,319 --> 00:01:51,159
your sister would rush

21
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:53,840
to transfer all the shares into her name.

22
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:58,359
You thought you could hide away

23
00:01:58,359 --> 00:02:00,599
and secretly squander the money,

24
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:04,359
never expecting you wouldn't get a dime.

25
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:07,280
Did the I Ching drive you crazy?

26
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:11,840
You really think you're some mastermind?

27
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:16,039
You could divine feng shui,

28
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:18,919
yet you

29
00:02:19,639 --> 00:02:21,319
could never read the human heart.

30
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:24,719
Your sister did that

31
00:02:25,319 --> 00:02:27,479
to protect your family's estate.

32
00:02:28,319 --> 00:02:29,360
But what about you?

33
00:02:31,599 --> 00:02:33,599
You thought she wanted to steal it all.

34
00:02:35,879 --> 00:02:36,759
One miscalculation.

35
00:02:38,439 --> 00:02:40,199
Never thought she'd crack so soon.

36
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:42,800
You don't believe in gods,

37
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:44,159
only in occult arts.

38
00:02:44,159 --> 00:02:45,039
Such a genius.

39
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:47,759
Too bad.

40
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,280
Life can't be calculated,

41
00:02:50,599 --> 00:02:52,479
nor is it ruled by trigrams and grids.

42
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:58,199
You're just a lunatic

43
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:00,319
poisoned to the bone with hate.

44
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:40,520
Look.

45
00:03:42,919 --> 00:03:43,719
Where?

46
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:54,400
Keep digging. Keep digging.

47
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:23,879
Open it.

48
00:04:45,319 --> 00:04:47,120
A drop on the tongue does the trick.

49
00:04:54,519 --> 00:04:55,639
Why did you pick this place?

50
00:04:57,399 --> 00:04:58,720
We used to live around here.

51
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:00,759
Back then, we'd always come here to dig wild greens.

52
00:05:01,199 --> 00:05:02,399
We were poor when I was a kid.

53
00:05:03,079 --> 00:05:04,720
For days every year, we had to

54
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:06,839
eat wild greens just to get by.

55
00:05:07,199 --> 00:05:10,040
We were poor, but I still miss those days.

56
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:11,480
In a way, they're coming home, too.

57
00:05:15,399 --> 00:05:17,519
Well, you let them return to their roots.

58
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:47,319
Xiao Chang.

59
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:52,360
What's wrong?

60
00:05:53,519 --> 00:05:54,519
The case is solved,

61
00:05:55,319 --> 00:05:56,240
and you got the commendation.

62
00:05:57,439 --> 00:05:58,920
Why the long face?

63
00:05:58,920 --> 00:05:59,720
What's going on?

64
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:01,360
It's not that,

65
00:06:02,279 --> 00:06:03,240
Captain Meng, Chief Shan.

66
00:06:03,439 --> 00:06:04,600
I'm not sulking.

67
00:06:07,519 --> 00:06:09,000
Something's weighing on my mind.

68
00:06:11,639 --> 00:06:12,480
I just can't wrap my head around it.

69
00:06:12,759 --> 00:06:13,519
I can't make sense of it.

70
00:06:14,079 --> 00:06:14,680
Let's hear it.

71
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:16,519
The case is solved,

72
00:06:16,519 --> 00:06:17,600
but the knot in my heart remains.

73
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:19,720
This commendation doesn't feel right.

74
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,040
Then I'll explain.

75
00:06:26,439 --> 00:06:28,959
I kept rewatching Hou Dong's confession.

76
00:06:30,279 --> 00:06:31,839
I still can't comprehend it.

77
00:06:32,759 --> 00:06:35,439
How could someone be so calm,

78
00:06:35,439 --> 00:06:38,040
almost methodical,

79
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:40,000
recounting how he murdered

80
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,959
and dismembered his own parents?

81
00:06:41,959 --> 00:06:42,519
I...

82
00:06:43,399 --> 00:06:44,319
I just don't get it.

83
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:45,600
I really don't.

84
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:50,920
It wasn't blind rage,

85
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:54,439
nor a momentary loss of control.

86
00:06:54,519 --> 00:06:55,639
That kind, I can understand.

87
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,319
To him, it was more like following steps,

88
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:02,920
carrying out some kind of

89
00:07:03,319 --> 00:07:03,839
mandatory ritual.

90
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:12,279
Looking at it in hindsight,

91
00:07:12,279 --> 00:07:13,120
all I feel

92
00:07:14,879 --> 00:07:15,680
is anger

93
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:17,319
and grief.

94
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,240
Yet I couldn't stop it.

95
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:20,839
I can't stop these crimes from happening.

96
00:07:20,839 --> 00:07:21,480
I just...

97
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:23,279
can't stop them.

98
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:25,720
It's this deep sense of powerlessness.

99
00:07:25,959 --> 00:07:26,920
Do you understand, Mentor?

100
00:07:30,079 --> 00:07:32,839
I despise the abusers and liars,

101
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:35,120
yet I grieve for victims like Sun Xiaofei,

102
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:36,360
whose lives were filled with misfortune.

103
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:38,879
I feel so torn, so powerless.

104
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:43,040
Xiao Chang.

105
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:46,360
The human heart...

106
00:07:51,199 --> 00:07:52,639
is harder to decipher

107
00:07:53,399 --> 00:07:54,360
than the toughest unsolved cases.

108
00:07:58,720 --> 00:07:59,560
When it comes to cases,

109
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:01,439
the more we deal with them,

110
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:04,920
the deeper we dig,

111
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:08,160
the more we realize that

112
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,360
there isn't just

113
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:12,120
black and white.

114
00:08:13,079 --> 00:08:15,600
There are shades we can never comprehend.

115
00:08:17,439 --> 00:08:18,319
Many answers

116
00:08:19,199 --> 00:08:20,319
the law can give you.

117
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:23,040
But what lies in the human heart...

118
00:08:24,759 --> 00:08:26,560
requires our own understanding,

119
00:08:26,879 --> 00:08:28,519
our own judgment.

120
00:08:29,399 --> 00:08:30,040
Understood.

121
00:08:31,079 --> 00:08:31,879
I understand.

122
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:35,360
I used to think the law was a scale

123
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:39,120
that weighs right and wrong,

124
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:40,639
measuring guilt and punishment.

125
00:08:42,399 --> 00:08:43,360
But now, I feel like

126
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:45,919
I've fallen into a labyrinth.

127
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:50,080
I hold the verdict of guilt in my hand,

128
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:51,440
plain as day.

129
00:08:53,639 --> 00:08:55,720
Yet when I look into the suspect's eyes,

130
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:56,559
at that very moment,

131
00:08:59,039 --> 00:09:02,080
I feel like their humanity has drowned.

132
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:05,960
Kid...

133
00:09:07,159 --> 00:09:08,240
You think too deeply,

134
00:09:08,639 --> 00:09:09,519
and you dig too far into things.

135
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:11,960
Sooner or later, you'll lose your mind.

136
00:09:12,559 --> 00:09:14,360
In our line of work, you must be observant,

137
00:09:14,759 --> 00:09:15,679
but your heart can't be too soft.

138
00:09:15,799 --> 00:09:16,759
And you definitely can't get sucked in.

139
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:20,759
I'll let you two talk, Old Meng.

140
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:24,320
He's got real potential. Guide him well.

141
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:25,240
Yes, sir.

142
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:35,039
Don't overthink it.

143
00:09:37,039 --> 00:09:38,679
No matter what, never forget

144
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,200
that we are police officers.

145
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:43,759
Our duty

146
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:46,960
is to get to the truth of the case,

147
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:49,879
bring criminals to justice,

148
00:09:51,039 --> 00:09:53,120
and maintain stability in society.

149
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,759
Fate is like a prison cell.

150
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:05,799
Who are we in it?

151
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:09,279
Are we the interrogators who enter,

152
00:10:09,279 --> 00:10:10,039
or are we

153
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:12,960
the ones trapped inside,

154
00:10:13,759 --> 00:10:16,080
never able to break free?

155
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:18,559
I don't know.

156
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:23,320
Fate.

157
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:35,279
What is it, Mentor?

158
00:10:36,279 --> 00:10:36,960
What's wrong?

159
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:42,080
It looks pretty ordinary.

160
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,200
Nothing special at all.

161
00:10:46,639 --> 00:10:47,480
Tell me.

162
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,360
How did you deduce it?

163
00:10:51,759 --> 00:10:54,000
There were no clues left at the scene.

164
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:56,159
Hou Dong didn't even mention it himself.

165
00:10:56,879 --> 00:10:58,159
How did you know?

166
00:10:59,919 --> 00:11:00,720
Explain.

167
00:11:01,639 --> 00:11:02,279
Mentor...

168
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:04,120
This is...

169
00:11:05,159 --> 00:11:07,279
It's really hard to explain.

170
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:10,399
Then give me a straight answer.

171
00:11:13,759 --> 00:11:15,759
I'm giving you a chance to explain right now.

172
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:19,559
I want you to explain it

173
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:22,879
in plain words that actually make sense.

174
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:25,399
Don't give me any crap about talent,

175
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,639
or gut feelings.

176
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:28,000
Criminal investigation...

177
00:11:29,039 --> 00:11:30,159
is a science.

178
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:32,039
It's logic.

179
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:35,519
It's a chain of evidence built bit by bit.

180
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,080
Not mysticism.

181
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,720
If you can explain this logically to me,

182
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:41,639
I'll buy it.

183
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:42,919
Go ahead.

184
00:11:50,639 --> 00:11:51,679
Put it this way...

185
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:56,360
It really wasn't deduction.

186
00:11:57,519 --> 00:11:58,960
With all these cases, you know,

187
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:00,879
it's like... like playing a movie.

188
00:12:00,879 --> 00:12:03,399
Flash—it just pops into your head.

189
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:05,039
Crystal clear.

190
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:06,080
Terrifyingly clear.

191
00:12:09,399 --> 00:12:10,720
Just pops into your head?

192
00:12:12,759 --> 00:12:13,480
What is that?

193
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:16,159
Are you playing psychic?

194
00:12:18,039 --> 00:12:19,720
Solving crimes isn't writing fiction.

195
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:22,519
Take last time, for instance.

196
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:25,440
Late at night, on Liu Jianguo's case,

197
00:12:26,639 --> 00:12:28,720
you said you saw something enter the woods.

198
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:29,600
I didn't see a thing.

199
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,000
I chased after you into the bamboo grove,

200
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:35,480
and damn if you didn't

201
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:39,399
actually dig up bloody clothes.

202
00:12:42,679 --> 00:12:44,360
Which dream did that come from?

203
00:12:46,679 --> 00:12:47,960
Can you explain that?

204
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:55,080
Mentor, I know it's hard to believe.

205
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:56,000
If I were in your shoes,

206
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,080
I wouldn't believe it either.

207
00:12:58,679 --> 00:13:00,559
That's why I've been looking for an answer.

208
00:13:01,799 --> 00:13:02,519
What answer?

209
00:13:04,519 --> 00:13:05,519
I don't know.

210
00:13:06,799 --> 00:13:09,279
I don't even know how I met you.

211
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:10,799
You don't know?

212
00:13:10,799 --> 00:13:11,519
I don't know either.

213
00:13:11,519 --> 00:13:13,240
Who pushed you onto me in the first place?

214
00:13:24,879 --> 00:13:26,559
Can you explain this to me?

215
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:30,639
Why?

216
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:33,240
Why did this happen?

217
00:13:39,639 --> 00:13:40,519
Trying to harm...

218
00:13:41,039 --> 00:13:42,279
Trying to kill me!

219
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:48,039
Don't move!

220
00:13:48,759 --> 00:13:49,360
Stay back!

221
00:13:49,360 --> 00:13:49,840
Put it down!

222
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:50,480
Stay back!

223
00:13:50,480 --> 00:13:51,320
Nobody move!

224
00:13:52,039 --> 00:13:52,840
Stay back!

225
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:54,000
Come any closer and I'll kill her!

226
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:54,799
Let the child go!

227
00:13:54,799 --> 00:13:55,600
Let go of her!

228
00:13:55,759 --> 00:13:56,080
Let go!

229
00:13:56,519 --> 00:13:57,279
Let the child go!

230
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:59,639
Come closer and I'll kill her!

231
00:13:59,639 --> 00:14:00,440
Let the kid go!

232
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:04,240
Drop it! Drop it!

233
00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:05,159
Drop the knife!

234
00:14:05,159 --> 00:14:05,759
Put it down!

235
00:14:05,919 --> 00:14:06,840
Drop the knife!

236
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:07,399
Drop it!

237
00:14:07,679 --> 00:14:08,600
Put it down!

238
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:11,960
Take him away! Take the knife!

239
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:13,320
Honey, wait for me!

240
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:14,039
Take him away!

241
00:14:14,039 --> 00:14:14,840
Honey!

242
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:17,200
Honey, wait for me!

243
00:14:36,039 --> 00:14:37,240
The little boy said

244
00:14:39,039 --> 00:14:40,399
on his way home from school,

245
00:14:41,519 --> 00:14:42,759
passing by the crime scene,

246
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:45,200
he heard some commotion.

247
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:48,480
Before his father died, he told him

248
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:52,200
never to approach a commotion outside.

249
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,840
He remembered his father's words.

250
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:56,679
He had no idea

251
00:14:58,639 --> 00:14:59,519
what that commotion was...

252
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:01,600
Lucky he didn't look.

253
00:15:04,559 --> 00:15:05,960
If it weren't for this case,

254
00:15:06,559 --> 00:15:07,360
the killer...

255
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:11,360
I wouldn't have let him live.

256
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,120
A family of three.

257
00:15:16,879 --> 00:15:18,360
The little girl is only six.

258
00:15:19,879 --> 00:15:21,159
At such a darling age.

259
00:15:23,919 --> 00:15:25,320
Good thing you didn't hesitate to shoot,

260
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:27,799
giving that little girl a fighting chance.

261
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:38,679
You're finally here.

262
00:15:40,200 --> 00:15:40,559
Sit.

263
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:42,120
Have a seat.

264
00:15:46,039 --> 00:15:48,080
Aren't you curious

265
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:49,919
why I killed their whole family?

266
00:15:51,679 --> 00:15:52,960
You sure are straightforward.

267
00:15:54,519 --> 00:15:55,279
Talk.

268
00:15:57,720 --> 00:16:00,559
The one you shot dead was my wife.

269
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:02,000
Her name was Du Lan.

270
00:16:02,559 --> 00:16:04,000
She was a dancer.

271
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,200
After the dance troupe disbanded,

272
00:16:07,159 --> 00:16:09,080
she taught kids at the Bureau of Culture.

273
00:16:09,799 --> 00:16:11,120
We were married for seven years.

274
00:16:12,919 --> 00:16:13,720
No kids.

275
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:16,559
Not that I didn't want any.

276
00:16:18,879 --> 00:16:19,960
She didn't want them.

277
00:16:21,080 --> 00:16:22,399
She wanted to keep her figure.

278
00:16:24,919 --> 00:16:26,320
She still dreamed of the stage.

279
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:28,240
I shot your wife.

280
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:30,759
Do you hate me?

281
00:16:35,919 --> 00:16:38,000
I'll be seeing my wife soon anyway.

282
00:16:39,159 --> 00:16:40,120
Down below,

283
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:42,720
we'll still be husband and wife.

284
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,559
When we did something like this,

285
00:16:51,919 --> 00:16:53,559
we never expected to make it out alive.

286
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:56,840
You're a long-haul truck driver.

287
00:16:59,080 --> 00:16:59,840
Hardworking.

288
00:17:00,759 --> 00:17:01,519
So,

289
00:17:02,279 --> 00:17:03,960
your family's living conditions

290
00:17:04,359 --> 00:17:05,240
were pretty decent.

291
00:17:05,559 --> 00:17:06,440
Decent enough.

292
00:17:08,319 --> 00:17:09,519
But my wife...

293
00:17:10,559 --> 00:17:12,480
My wife was way out of my league.

294
00:17:13,279 --> 00:17:14,160
Young.

295
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:15,119
Pretty.

296
00:17:17,319 --> 00:17:19,039
Her marrying me,

297
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:22,400
I felt really lucky.

298
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:25,960
Sometimes I even felt

299
00:17:27,759 --> 00:17:30,160
I'd used up a lifetime of luck on her.

300
00:17:32,839 --> 00:17:33,720
Sorry.

301
00:17:34,839 --> 00:17:36,599
I'm rambling a bit.

302
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:39,640
I rarely talk to anyone driving long-haul.

303
00:17:41,359 --> 00:17:42,319
But rest assured.

304
00:17:44,559 --> 00:17:46,359
I'll tell you every single detail,

305
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:49,240
the whole story from start to finish.

306
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:50,119
Don't worry.

307
00:17:51,839 --> 00:17:52,359
Yeah.

308
00:17:52,599 --> 00:17:53,200
By the way,

309
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:56,119
can this case

310
00:17:57,039 --> 00:17:58,160
make the news?

311
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:02,720
Or on the internet.

312
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:05,079
You committed such a heinous crime,

313
00:18:05,279 --> 00:18:06,359
and you're proud?

314
00:18:08,279 --> 00:18:09,519
It's deeply satisfying!

315
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,559
I want scumbags everywhere

316
00:18:14,559 --> 00:18:15,960
to see this news

317
00:18:16,839 --> 00:18:18,599
and never get hard again.

318
00:18:30,359 --> 00:18:32,240
Lift your head. Sit up straight.

319
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:37,240
Talk.

320
00:18:38,039 --> 00:18:40,359
Tell me about this bitter grudge of yours.
